# Spec-driven development

Use OpenSpec + lidr-specboot for planned feature work. Do not copy `lidr-specboot/docs/` into Mattermost `docs/`.

## Command flow

1. `/enrich-us` — refine the user story
2. `/ff` (or `/opsx-ff`) — create OpenSpec artifacts
3. `/apply` (or `/opsx-apply`) — implement tasks one by one
4. `/verify` (or `/opsx-verify`) — check code against artifacts
5. `/adversarial-review` — independent review before archive
6. `/archive` (or `/opsx-archive`)
7. `/commit`

## Sources of truth

- Workflow: `openspec/config.yaml`, `lidr-specboot/docs/base-standards.md`
- Tasks checklist: `lidr-specboot/docs/openspec-tasks-mandatory-steps.md`
- Course story: `user_stories.md`
- Mattermost code rules: `server/AGENTS.md`, `webapp/AGENTS.md`

Treat lidr-specboot backend/frontend docs as TDD/process guidance only. Follow existing Go/React patterns in this repo.

If a change is requested after `/apply` and before `/archive`, update OpenSpec artifacts first, then code.
